    {
      "path": "runtimes/codex/app-server-client.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/runtimes/codex/app-server-client.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "6cfb2582a9beb597e5621e299a0463cdb234c808fab03f6874a509852dd62956",
      "vendoredSha256": "3c5cc6e2f16df900abafe50fa6eb8d76126a88dfb5c516f87b12d0727746781f",
      "delta": "Caller-owned process: the injected LineProcess spawn receives exactly the explicit filtered env, cwd and launch arguments; no ambient env merge, home-initialization queue, executable manager, resources reader or killTree option. Server requests: numeric and string ids preserved; result and error replies go through the acknowledged stdin write. Terminal state: an exit or a kill sets one sticky terminal error, with the bounded, redacted exitError of the BYOK transport on exit; it settles every pending request as exited at once, rejects later requests and writes, and ignores later lines. No per-request deadline and no count budget: operation deadlines live in the SDK Codex adapter, and the BYOK transport bounds line bytes."
    },
