    {
      "path": "runtimes/codex/session.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/runtimes/codex/session.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "b07c31ed744abe598c6121c3ad471f830014a7a08471a14941da7c327ff875a0",
      "vendoredSha256": "790e14584d63fc1e4cb9f2b8107adb8cfab0a58ec073121c4e1dda5cba03d310",
      "delta": "Raw adapter for the SDK: injected spawn and a required explicit filtered env; caller-selected sandboxMode (danger-full-access default, inherit passes no override) instead of ambient OAR_CODEX_SANDBOX; returns AdapterSession without sealSession/withSessionCredentials/observe, building one sessionCredentialRedactor per open as the kernel redact hook and for errors from the open path and every control. The upstream kernel is created with that redactor, and the onRecord hook is registered as a kernel observer before any record is appended. Native-first recording: each notification is retained as a body.origin=\"byok-native\" frame before the fold; a fold failure kills the process visibly. Server requests: caller-owned bounded native interaction lifecycle when configured, else synchronous decline/-32601 rejection under a 1000ms dispatch deadline; on-request approval policy is verified in the open reply. Owned process lifetime: spawn/adoption settles before the first write, failed initialization kills. Codex steer is a required member."
    },
